  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The equilibrium constant for the reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>Sn</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>20</mn></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The magnitude of standard electrode potential of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sn</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>*</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Zn</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>76</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
  },
